  "description": "The environmental sustainability and geography major encompasses the natural sciences, social sciences, and humanities in order to give students a broad understanding of the relationships between people, places, and the environment. Graduates of this program are prepared to understand complex human-environment and societal issues and to promote the flourishing of communities, regions, and the environment. Students choosing the sustainability concentration follow careers ranging from environmental law to environmental management to sustainability analysts for governments and corporations.",
